---
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";

const title = "Hi, I'm Bruce.";
---

<BaseLayout title={title}>
  <p>A frontend web developer, ui engineer, drummer, and wannabe pilot living in the south east of England.</p>
  <p>I try my best to build web solutions that are <a href="https://resilientwebdesign.com/">resilient</a>, <a href="https://trentwalton.com/2014/03/10/device-agnostic/">usable</a> and as future-friendly as possible. For this reason I prefer a vanilla approach and tend to be fairly tech-agnostic.</p>
  <h2>What's this website about?</h2>
  <p>This could turn out to be a version of my main site (<a href="https://brootaylor.com">brootaylor.com</a>) using the Astro web framework.</p>
  <p>More than likely this will serve up specific content that I'd like to render on a subdomain of my main site, such as a portfolio or CV/resume.</p>
  <p>Or... I may make this into an experimental playground area for all sorts of web development ideas, techniques, features, etc.</p>
  <p>I guess we'll see. 🤔</p>
</BaseLayout>
